The collision preset, G1 motor/posture configuration and command-progress
curriculum are adapted from mjlab (https://github.com/mujocolab/mjlab),
commit 8bb2bc9e187797689ec82c78c35019afd2fd0376, licensed under Apache-2.0.
See the repository LICENSE for the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Adaptations include Gobot scene serialization, preserved articulated hands with
fixed targets, explicit multi-shape foot groups, and CPU/Warp batch execution.
The original Unitree meshes/MJCF are supplied separately by the user and are
not included in this derived preset.

Motion preprocessing and validation design were cross-checked against:
- supermimic_vibed, a1508d42c9d1699a52e8233ab16d08c488441ab9 (MIT).
- Uni-SuperMimic, faf7818 (Apache-2.0, preserving the upstream MIT notice).
No Isaac Lab or UniLab runtime is imported by this Gobot task.

AMP loss and style reward: Peng et al., "AMP: Adversarial Motion Priors for
Stylized Physics-Based Character Control", SIGGRAPH 2021, equations 7-8.
SuperMimic reference: Liao et al., arXiv:2610.28480, 2026. The world-model
algorithm is not implemented here; it informed reference-data and contract checks.

Downloaded LAFAN1/G1 data remains a separate, untracked asset. Its source,
revision, checksums, and license are retained in assets/motions/source.json.
